# Autoploidy and Alloploidy

=== layout: one-panel

# *Types of Polyploids*

@body

- An [*autopolyploid*]{underline=true} is an individual with more than two chromosome sets, derived from a [_single_]{underline=true} species
- An [*allopolyploid*]{underline=true} is a species with multiple sets of chromosomes derived from [_different_]{underline=true} species
  - A combination of chromosome sets from different species.
  - Allopolyploid plant species are much more numerous than autopolyploids.

